      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. To go a bit deeper, we're seeing cases where the lesions have these strange, nodular, almost bumpy textures that don't follow typical epidermal patterns. Do you have specific guidance on when to shift from a general dermatosis code to something more specific when the physical presentation is particularly irregular or \"unusual\" in its shape and texture? We want to avoid the L89 or similar non-specific coding when the morphology is clearly abnormal.",
